<!--
  English Translation File — NFR-009.3 (Bilingual Support)
  ==========================================================
  NFR-009.3: English language translation strings
    This JSON file contains all English text strings used across
    the public-facing frontend. Translated to Sesotho in st.json.

  Structure:
    - nav: Navigation menu items
    - hero: Homepage hero section content
    - why: "Why Choose Us" feature descriptions
    - products: Product category names
    - how: "How It Works" step descriptions
    - testimonials: Testimonial section title
    - cta: Call-to-action section text
    - footer: Footer section text
    - auth: Login/signup form labels
    - shop: Shopping cart and checkout labels
    - contact: Contact form labels

  Usage:
    - lang.js reads this file and applies translations based on data-i18n attributes
    - Language selection persisted in localStorage (key: 'lang')
    - Toggle button calls toggleLanguage() to switch between en.json and st.json

  NFR-009.3 Design Notes:
    - Hierarchical JSON structure mirrors DOM structure for easy mapping
    - Keys use dot notation (e.g., "hero.badge") matching data-i18n="hero.badge"
    - All translatable UI text included; no hardcoded strings in HTML
    - Fallback: if translation key missing, original HTML text is preserved
-->